# Nightly — the standard unattended run.
#
# id | title | script | enable-var | requires | on-fail | timeout-var
#
# `script` is a path under `stages/`, and the folder is the **domain** it verifies — see
# stages/README.md. Adding a capability adds a folder and its rows; it never edits the engine.
#
# ⚠️ ORDER IS DELIBERATE, in three bands:
#   1. cheap and static first, so a broken tree is known within minutes rather than at dawn;
#   2. deployment integrity BEFORE anything rebuilds an image, or a legitimate rebuild reads as drift;
#   3. the long measurements last, so waking early still finds the quick answers already written.
#
# Only `preflight` aborts. Everything else records its failure and lets the night continue, because
# one broken thing should not cost you the other six answers.
# `requires` accepts stage ids, or the token `always` — which means "run even if the run
# aborted". Only the report uses it: an aborted night is the one that most needs a written summary.

preflight            | Pre-flight checks                 | platform/preflight.sh   | RUN_PREFLIGHT            |           | abort    | TIMEOUT_PREFLIGHT
gate                 | Production gate                   | platform/gate.sh        | RUN_GATE                 | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_GATE
deployment           | Deployment integrity              | platform/deployment.sh  | RUN_DEPLOYMENT           | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_DEPLOYMENT
boundary             | Contracts and perception boundary | platform/boundary.sh    | RUN_BOUNDARY             | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_BOUNDARY
runtime              | Real inference, end to end        | runtime/inference.sh    | RUN_RUNTIME              | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_RUNTIME
dashboard            | Operator page in a browser        | runtime/dashboard.sh    | RUN_DASHBOARD            | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_DASHBOARD
integration          | Cross-service integration tests   | platform/integration.sh | RUN_INTEGRATION          | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_INTEGRATION
tracking             | Object tracking, end to end       | tracking/tracking.sh    | RUN_TRACKING             | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_TRACKING
tracking-deployment  | Tracking as deployed              | tracking/deployment.sh  | RUN_TRACKING_DEPLOYMENT  | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_TRACKING
tracking-browser     | Track pages in a browser          | tracking/browser.sh     | RUN_TRACKING_BROWSER     | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_TRACKING_BROWSER
event-bridge         | Live event bridge, end to end     | events/bridge.sh        | RUN_EVENT_BRIDGE         | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_EVENT_BRIDGE
event-replay         | Duplicates, correlation, replay   | events/replay.sh        | RUN_EVENT_REPLAY         | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_EVENT_REPLAY
event-browser        | Event bridge page in a browser    | events/browser.sh       | RUN_EVENT_BROWSER        | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_EVENT_BROWSER
# ── Camera Processing Assignment (P-8 Phase 6) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️ `assignment` carries the milestone's central invariant: three cameras record, ONE is
# assigned, and the other two must analyse nothing. Every stage above proves the platform can
# analyse a camera; only this one proves it can decline to.
assignment           | Camera assignment, end to end      | assignment/assignment.sh | RUN_ASSIGNMENT           | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_ASSIGNMENT
assignment-runtime   | Runtime health, capacity, failover | assignment/runtime.sh    | RUN_ASSIGNMENT_RUNTIME   | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_ASSIGNMENT_RUNTIME
assignment-browser   | Assignment pages in a browser      | assignment/browser.sh    | RUN_ASSIGNMENT_BROWSER   | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_ASSIGNMENT_BROWSER
stability            | Stability run                     | runtime/stability.sh    | RUN_SOAK                 | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_SOAK
benchmark            | Capacity ladder and benchmark     | runtime/benchmark.sh    | RUN_BENCHMARK            | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_BENCHMARK
tracking-benchmark   | Tracking capacity ladder          | tracking/benchmark.sh   | RUN_TRACKING_BENCHMARK   | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_TRACKING_BENCHMARK
assignment-benchmark | Assignment capacity ladder         | assignment/benchmark.sh  | RUN_ASSIGNMENT_BENCHMARK | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_ASSIGNMENT_BENCHMARK
publisher-benchmark  | Publisher capacity ladder         | publisher/benchmark.sh  | RUN_PUBLISHER_BENCHMARK  | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_PUBLISHER_BENCHMARK
mutation             | Mutation verification             | runtime/mutation.sh     | RUN_MUTATION             | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_MUTATION
tracking-mutations   | Tracking mutation verification    | tracking/mutations.sh   | RUN_TRACKING_MUTATION    | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_TRACKING_MUTATION
assignment-mutations | Assignment mutation verification   | assignment/mutations.sh  | RUN_ASSIGNMENT_MUTATION  | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_ASSIGNMENT_MUTATION
bridge-mutations     | Bridge mutation verification      | publisher/mutations.sh  | RUN_BRIDGE_MUTATION      | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_BRIDGE_MUTATION
# ⚠️ LAST before the report, and not by accident: this is the only stage that stops the broker every
# service on the platform shares. Anything scheduled after it would be measuring a stack that had
# just been degraded on purpose, and would fail for a reason belonging to this row.
broker-resilience    | Broker outage and recovery        | broker/resilience.sh    | RUN_BROKER_RESILIENCE    | preflight | continue | TIMEOUT_BROKER_RESILIENCE
report               | Morning summary                   | platform/report.sh      | RUN_REPORT               | always    | continue | TIMEOUT_REPORT
